    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for May 28th centers on a high-ceiling core facing favorable matchups, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.16) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.81). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** earns our highest mark of the day; despite the lineup pending status, his underlying xwOBA (.378) combined with a favorable park boost and the expectation of hitting in the two-hole positions him to exploit Chris Bassitt\u2019s middling xERA. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a traditional platoon disadvantage against Patrick Corbin, his overall talent profile and the 16% park adjustment override the negative platoon split. **Coby Mayo** (66.72) is also a strong start today, as he effectively leverages the platoon advantage against the lefty Corbin, signaling a significant power-outage opportunity in the middle of the order.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was between **Josh Jung** (63.10) and **Miguel Vargas** (60.21). Ultimately, **Josh Jung** earned the final starting slot due to his cleaner projection against Spencer Arrighetti, whereas **Miguel Vargas** suffered a slight downward revision due to marginal platoon dynamics against the starting pitcher. We continue to monitor the bench for impact, but the delta was sufficient to favor **Josh Jung**'s volume in the heart of the order. \n\nAs we manage our limited daily game caps, we are keeping a close watch on **Dominic Smith**, who fell below our efficiency floor of 40.0. His score was depressed by a poor L/L platoon matchup and a 35% rain risk in his venue, making him an easy bench decision. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined, our focus remains on maximizing the efficiency of our active core, particularly looking for **Sam Antonacci** to provide the necessary spark on the basepaths against a targetable Woods Richardson. All lineup-pending designations remain speculative, and we will adjust if confirmed spots deviate significantly from our projections.",
